<title>UK: Farmer tells robbers his hemp won't get them high.</title>
<headline>Farmer tells robbers his hemp won't get them high.</headline>
<dateline>LYMINGTON, England 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British farmer George Heathcote, distraught that people were stealing his hemp crop after mistaking it for cannabis, put up a huge sign on Friday to warn them off.</p>
<p>&quot;You would have to smoke a joint the size of a telegraph pole to get stoned,&quot; the sign in southern England said.</p>
</text>
